# Nohello Hide Rule System
#
# Each line = a directory to cover with an empty tmpfs in target apps'
# mount namespaces, so anti-cheat probes of CHILD paths under it fail
# (ENOENT). The directory itself still resolves.
#
# Default (built-in, always applied first):
#   /sys/module   (kernel module enumeration — KernelSU / kp-next traces)
#
# Optional per-line SELinux context: "<path> context=<context>"
#
# ⚠️ Notes:
#   - /dev/pts covering breaks openpty()/pts allocation in apps — do NOT add
#     it unless the target app never allocates PTYs.
#   - /sys/class/kgsl covering can break the game's own GPU monitoring
#     (Unreal reads kgsl nodes for perf/thermal). Add only when spoofing a
#     MediaTek donor (which has no kgsl) AND the game tolerates it.
#
# Uncomment to add more:
# /sys/class/kgsl
